# Banned terms for scripts/check-banned-terms.sh (make check-banned-terms).
#
# Copy this file to .banned-terms.local and put the real terms there. Git ignores that file,
# so the terms are never published. This example holds no real term.
#
# One term per line. Blank lines and lines that start with # are ignored.
# Matching is literal (not a regular expression) and ignores upper and lower case.
# It covers file contents and file names. Nothing under app/ is checked.
#
# A copy of this file unchanged has no terms in it, and the check then FAILS on purpose:
# a check with no terms has checked nothing.
#
# example-term-one
# example term two
